    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d88">

                <pb facs="0161" n="995" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v02/pg995"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 600.119/1026</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        French Deputy High Commissioner</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Billy</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-09-17">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">September 17, 1918</hi>.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. de Billy</hi>: I
                    acknowledge the receipt of your letter of July 16<anchor n="1" xml:id="d88-f1"/>
                    in which you inform me that the French Government would be pleased to learn the
                    attitude of this Government towards certain commercial treaties entered into
                    between the Imperial German Government and some of the neutral governments and
                    containing stipulations relative to trade after the war.</p>
                <p>In reply, I beg to advise you that this Government is not at the present time
                    prepared to define its attitude towards the treaties in question.</p>
                <p>I am [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert Lansing</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
